0  years in both media and in the industry  you know a heavy heavy black listing  that I somehow managed to survive and  get a job on a TV show so I could fight  my way through it one of the benefits of  being on that TV shows that was popular  all over the world and so I knew when it  came time to strike that it would be  newsworthy you'd be predators being that  the force behind the me2 movement though  that we talked about in it it it it grew  very very quickly didn't it we were you  surprised by how quickly it was picked  up on across the world  I am so immensely proud of that you know  I think  - what Tirana Berk started was amazing  with a hashtag that just gives us a way  to actually communicate about something  that happened to us it's not like  there's a bunch of women with pitchforks  running after you know executives me too  is fundamentally at its heart just about  a shared experience in a way for people  that have survived this and there's an  awful lot of us men and women who  survive this to have a way to talk to  each other about it you know and I am  immensely proud of how far it spread and  and it just needs to be given time to  breathe you know what I mean we've never  been here before in society I wanted to  change the cultural landscape and the  cultural conversation and so I'm really  glad that we're all having this very  adult conversation that needed to be had  well you can send that it's being  devalued sometimes that there have been  some people who've used it and they've  you know for perhaps that you know  somebody at work inappropriately asking  them out for a date or something  something they feel is inappropriate but  when you compare it to your experience  or the experience of a lot of women  who've been physically sexually and  mentally abused do you feel that that  there's a danger that it devalues  perhaps some of the worst excesses I  think it's again it's about having a  collective conversation and setting  boundaries and not knee-jerk reactions  but understanding you know we all know  the difference we're we're adults we  know the difference you know when you're  younger you don't necessarily not offend  for yourself and it doesn't mean that as  an adult you don't get attacked my point  is just that that conversation about  someone asking not to dinner which I  don't think you know I hope that doesn't  really happen but if someone is offended  by that then they can say that and they  can set boundaries right then and there  there's also of course Asia Argento and  and she you know was a friend of yours  and was also very part of the meteor  campaign there's been this whole story  about her and Jimmy Bennett now we  you're not going to go into who's right  or who's wrong and who says what and  that but has that in it anyway sullied  the the me2 movement do you think you  know the me2 movement again it's just  about a shared experience so I don't  think there's anything that anybody can  do to take that away I have so many  people that stopped me on the street or  send me messages on insta  you know and they talked to me about  it's the first time they've ever told  anybody and there's a lot of boys and  men in that group I include and I don't  think so you know I think it's a  personal setback and a setback for it's  it's shocking and dismaying but I think  you know this is a strong movement and  this is a way for women and and other  victims to stand up and be counted and I  don't think that can be taken away now  do you we surprised at all by the level  of vitriol that you presumably had been  at the receiving end of since since this  came up the be level of anger there is  against women who stand up and speak out  I was very aware before I spoke because  I helped set the articles up the New  York Times and I'm the first one to go  on the record I went on the record of  NBC even though they sat on it for many  months I knew it was going to be a huge  backlash and as somebody who was sold 